      "Their names are known. Most are not. Drones in Sudan are flown into markets, homes, power stations and camps for the displaced, hundreds of kilometres from any front line. The machines that do this are built abroad, paid for abroad and flown into Sudan along routes that were mapped this year by United Nations investigators.",
