      "In El Obeid, North Kordofan, nine RSF drone strikes between June and August 2026 were investigated by Amnesty International. Thirty-seven civilians were killed and ten were injured. Amnesty's researchers could identify no military target near any of the places at the time they were hit. On 5 February 2026, at least twelve civilians were injured when army drones struck the Soug El Na'am market in West Kordofan. On 21 November, homes, the airport and a UN building with staff inside were hit by drones in Khartoum, and four people were killed. The strikes were attributed to the RSF; the army blamed Ethiopia for the drones.",
