      "What follows separates what has been established from what has only been claimed, and names who said each thing. A finding is a conclusion reached by a UN body. An investigation is evidence gathered and published by a named rights group, research group or news organisation. A claim is an allegation not yet independently verified, labelled with whoever made it. Every denial is printed beside the claim it answers.",
